{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To deliver you.</b> That is, that He will deliver you completely in war, and not a single man of you will be missing, as occurred in the war against Midian, where it is written (Numbers 31:49): ״ולא נפקד ממנו איש״ — 'and not one was missing from us.' For it is the way of the world among the other nations that even when they are victorious, many of them perish; but in a war of obligation (milchemet mitzvah) they will be altogether victorious, and not a single one of them will die there. Therefore Joshua cried out when about thirty-six men fell from them, and our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: this was Yair ben Menasheh, who was equivalent to the majority of the Sanhedrin."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:37.084546658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}